  "rewrites": {
   "5": {
    "original": "The fund was brought about in an effort to accelerate commercialisation in local companies, as well as to attract foreign industries to establish presence in Singapore and tap on the attractive pool of scientific talent here.",
    "rewrite": "The initiative aims to speed up commercialization within local firms and also strives to lure foreign industries by establishing a presence in Singapore, leveraging the robust pool of scientific talent available."
   },
   "8": {
    "original": "Mr Wee was speaking to Channel NewsAsia during the Harvard Business School (HBS) Alumni Association of Singapore General Assembly held at ALAMO Restaurant.",
    "rewrite": "Mr Wee was interviewed by Channel NewsAsia at the ALAMO Restaurant during the Harvard Business School (HBS) Alumni Association of Singapore General Assembly."
   },
   "2": {
    "original": "DeClout is Asia's biggest marketer of patents and intellectual property, and currently has over a dozen runway companies in its ventures division.",
    "rewrite": "DeClout serves as the largest marketer of patents and intellectual property in Asia, with presently more than a dozen runway companies under its ventures division."
   },
   "1": {
    "original": "The fund aims to accelerate commercialisation of technologies by early stage venture capital companies to attract global and regional industries.",
    "rewrite": "The fund seeks to speed up the commercialization of technologies for early stage venture capital firms to attract both local and international industries."
   },
   "10": {
    "original": "In the absence of chairperson, he is stepping in to lead the Innovation Circle to plan events and the Innovation Circle Month occurring in June.",
    "rewrite": "When the chairperson is unavailable, he will step in to lead the Innovation Circle in planning events and the Innovation Circle Month in June."
   },
   "4": {
    "original": "In return, DeClout would contribute additional funding to whittle down the risk of the financial support for the local companies.",
    "rewrite": "Consequently, DeClout would provide extra financing to reduce the financial risk for the local businesses."
   },
   "9": {
    "original": "Mr Wee is also Co-Chairperson of the Innovation Circle of the HBS Club of Singapore in a volunteer role.",
    "rewrite": "Mr Wee also holds the position of Co-Chairperson of the Innovation Circle of the HBS Club of Singapore on a voluntary basis."
   },
   "3": {
    "original": "Last year, it committed to an S$85-million venture capital fund for companies in which it had invested.",
    "rewrite": "Last year, it vowed to dedicate an S$85-million venture capital fund to firms it had stakes in."
   }
  },
  "final_span": "the 15 local companies receiving the fund. The fund seeks to speed up the commercialization of technologies for early stage venture capital firms to attract both local and international industries.\nDeClout serves as the largest marketer of patents and intellectual property in Asia, with presently more than a dozen runway companies under its ventures division. Last year, it vowed to dedicate an S$85-million venture capital fund to firms it had stakes in.\nConsequently, DeClout would provide extra financing to reduce the financial risk for the local businesses. The initiative aims to speed up commercialization within local firms and also strives to lure foreign industries by establishing a presence in Singapore, leveraging the robust pool of scientific talent available.\nAt the NRF Venture Summit on May 4, Chairman of DeClout, Patrick Wee, said: \"This is the third of its kind and we would definitely like to be part of another third of the fund. Renewing the assistance would increase our time and effort in developing these start-up companies into what we expect them to be and what we are capable of doing.\"\nMr Wee was interviewed by Channel NewsAsia at the ALAMO Restaurant during the Harvard Business School (HBS) Alumni Association of Singapore General Assembly.\nMr Wee also holds the position of Co-Chairperson of the Innovation Circle of the HBS Club of Singapore on a voluntary basis. When the chairperson is unavailable, he will step in to lead the Innovation Circle in planning events and the Innovation Circle Month in June.\nMr Wee said, \"We discussed with the HBS Club of Singapore what the students could do, to make sure that their learning takes place whilst recognising that Singapore has its challenges. If we want to develop these start-ups, we all need to work with the government, its agencies, as well as the public and private sector involved in these developments and bringing these companies into the public eye, and into the limelight so that the general knowledge of the group and the plurality, not just of venture capitalists but of the general population can benefit from some of the new investments that are being made in Singapore especially in areas of big data, analytics, Internet of Things (IoT)",
  "break_point": null
 },
